     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I have a covariate that has values between 0 and 1. and it contains missing values.</div><div>I want to set a uniform prior for the missing values using the &#39;“<a href=\"https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/_book/Toolbox.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/_book/Toolbox.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462443868000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2At1wHee6vFPHNnx2F_qTC\">transformation trick</a>” .</div><div>But it gives an error in pnorm(). Here is a sample of the code i used:<br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>PARAMETER_VECTOR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">u</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>DATA_INTEGER</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Nmiss</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> missing</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Nmiss</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nll </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> nll </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">u</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#008\">true</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br> missing </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> pnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">u</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#008\">true</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span></div></code></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font> Does anyone have an idea about the error. Thanks for your help.</div></div>"
